  <ym-title|Actual uniform slab-copy producer><label|actual-uniform-slab-copy-producer>

  Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  Author: parent <verbatim|hairer-codex-existence-20261111>, within #26
  confirmed claim. Authoritative text: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-slab-copy-bounds.tex>.
  Status: draft; independent source/mathematical review pending.

  <section|Scope and same-data interfaces><label|scope-and-same-data-interfaces>

  Supplies the actual Bench/AllCopy application from the same Seed.CellHyp,
  Makes, Hierarchy, PointLimits and gentle mesh. Does not choose another
  hierarchy or assume the requested slab-copy estimate. Does not supply
  rotation actions, phase grid approximants or corrected detector moments.
  Canonical centered service, coarse one-field bracketing/copied-orbit
  argument, finite planted inequality and generic smooth point limits are
  retained inputs. The same expanding mesh-then-period order is used
  throughout. Each-period CenteredBook is unnecessary here. Local inputs
  remain subject to whole-proof closure and human acceptance; this local
  draft does not certify them.

  <section|Inspected source crosswalk><label|inspected-source-crosswalk>

  All paths below are under <verbatim|Lean/YM/> at the pinned revision.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Prose
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified declarations /
  source>>>|<row|<cell|Uniform bounded multiplet prices, including finite
  signed orbit>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.rates>, immediate private
  mirror_ball/one_grade; <verbatim|Next/PHASE/Seats.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Exact
  centered input with additive tolerance and common late
  order>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Cells.CellHyp.centered>,
  <verbatim|Cells/Packing.lean>; <verbatim|YM.Extraction.centeredBudget>,
  <verbatim|Wcmain.projects>, <verbatim|CenterPort.book>,
  <verbatim|Extraction/Center.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Coarse root of an exterior
  group and mixed planted bound>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.exterior_group>,
  <verbatim|cutoff_bound>, <verbatim|Single>, <verbatim|Single.moves>,
  <verbatim|Next/PHASE/Roots.lean>; aligned margin/reflection helpers in
  <verbatim|Aligned.lean>; reused Lease.alive one-field argument already in
  centered-estimates>>|<row|<cell|Finitely many residue patterns,
  perturbations and ordered continuum limit>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.Pattern>,
  <verbatim|Gapped>, <verbatim|point_bound>, immediate
  margins/numeric_bound/round_same/round_near,
  <verbatim|Next/PHASE/Passage.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Counts 4qn and 2 exterior
  copies, q-independent exterior price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.travel_price>,
  immediate train_buffer/train_length/ride_train/train_suit/words_bound,
  <verbatim|Next/PHASE/Trains.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Fourth-power mesh lower
  bound and uniform n/r price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.replicas>,
  immediate room_for/ext_room, <verbatim|Next/PHASE/Seats.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.OS.thickness>, <verbatim|turn>, <verbatim|At>,
  <verbatim|OS/Halves.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Positive integral sub-width chosen
  before exterior>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.narrow>, <verbatim|Covered>,
  <verbatim|OS/Halves.lean>; <verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.seats>,
  <verbatim|Seats.lean>; exact <verbatim|YM.Bid.Bench>, <verbatim|Seats>,
  <verbatim|Bid/Phase.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Repetition bound and bounded
  operator>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.QRead>, <verbatim|producer>,
  <verbatim|OS/Train.lean>; canonical manuscript Lemma
  ex-train-bound>>|<row|<cell|Padding by remaining heat time, unique common
  Spread>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.B01.answer>, immediate with_cost,
  <verbatim|Work/B01.lean>; <verbatim|YM.OS.Spread.radius>,
  <verbatim|AllCopy>, <verbatim|OS/Slabs.lean>>>>>>

  The manuscript groups the geometric helpers by their actual mathematical
  purpose. It explains the mixed coarse/fine root argument, including
  multiple exterior fields in a single coarse cell, rather than assuming
  products of coarse one-field norms. It explicitly keeps independent
  perturbations of replica slots before generic point-limit passage;
  convergence is not assumed on a congruent-pattern submanifold or projection
  ties.

  <section|Literature and checks><label|literature-and-checks>

  Searched shared background catalog and available notes (README and
  su2-simplicity); no applicable source-specific two-scale same-family
  result. The needed planted/centered and bounded-operator arguments already
  have canonical manuscript proofs and are reused. No new external theorem is
  asserted, and no broad literature search was undertaken for this bounded
  source-specialization task.

  Commands actually run: focused cat/sed/rg reads of the files listed above
  and canonical centered-estimates, selected-centered-service, phases and
  phase regularity/producers; sha256sum on the new prose. No Lean changes,
  fresh Lean build or axiom replay. TeX integration/build/visual QA and
  independent review are pending at this snapshot. The exact displayed
  exponent is K=4(D+1), with constants selected before word length, slab
  width, buffer, exterior or copies.

